WEBVTT

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.280
Where am I?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.730
Who am I?

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.440
Do you want to know who you are?

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.480
If you do, I'll tell you.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.400
I'll tell you who you are,
and what you want.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.190
What I want?

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.610
<i>Howl at the Moon</i> .
The author is Sakutaro Hagiwara.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.230
I see.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:18.400
So what we're seeing here is all of his
unique worlds blended into one place.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.530
Why do you keep following me?

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.780
What did I do?

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.070
He's chasing you. That strange dog.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.280
Yup. It's a strange dog.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.480
Did you know?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.610
Animals can instinctively sense if
another creature is weaker than them.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.570
I see.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.030
So that's why it's following Dazai- <i>kun</i> ?

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.780
What does that mean?

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.360
What?

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.150
The sound of a pistol?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.530
That's...

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.730
Chuya!

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.160
"Episode 5"

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.980
Chuya! Chuya!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.320
What do you want?

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.070
You scared me!

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.070
I thought you were dead!

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:12.780
Well, I think I am, actually.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.610
Don't be weird.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.530
Dead people don't talk.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.780
You really dead, Chuya?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.730
I am!

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.110
But then how can you answer him?

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.280
Is he an evil spirit?

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.110
No!

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:34.730
One possibility... would be that you've died
as part of the events of this book.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.820
You're so smart!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.360
Let's go with that!

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.610
Oww!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.820
Let him go, would you?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.570
Be a good boy.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.400
Huh? Sensei?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.980
Look, I really don't care.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.820
But can you do something?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.480
I can't move.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.280
Of course you can't. You're dead.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.820
How's it feel to go to hell?

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.280
Hey, don't just assume I'm going to hell!

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.030
And don't treat me like I'm dead
just because I'm a corpse.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.400
Oh no. This is going to be annoying.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.730
I'd like to help, but what can we do?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.070
We could dig him a grave.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.780
Don't bury me!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.780
It may be better to solve
what's going on here.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.190
Solve it?

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.570
Find the killer, for example.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:28.610
Yes, if he was shot,
someone must have shot him.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.230
And we're supposed to find him?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.030
The killer's the Taint, right?

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.610
Yes.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.190
But it's not that simple.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.980
What do you mean?

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.400
The fact that we were all captured
the moment we delved.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.190
The strange things that
happened without warning.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:53.320
Taken together, they imply that that the
Taint is manipulating the world itself.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.190
Manipulating the world?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.610
Is that possible?

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.780
I've never heard of it happening.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.820
Either something extraordinary
is happening, or...

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.940
Hey, I may be a corpse, but that
doesn't mean you can ignore me!

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.730
Anyway, the one way we've got

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:15.530
to get close to the Taint is solve
the mysteries in front of us.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:18.820
Okay, I'll be the detective!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:23.190
I don't know if this is "okay" or not,
but I appreciate the enthusiasm.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.610
Go get 'em, Dazai.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.400
You're my assistant.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.030
Listen, stop playing around.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.980
This is a murder! Treat it like one!

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:36.320
Sorry. It's hard to take a
talking corpse seriously.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:39.610
We can probably assume the
pistol's the murder weapon.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.190
Nope, Ango.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.900
You have to start by
questioning your assumptions.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.230
So what else could it be?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.320
The real murder weapon...

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.110
...is this chair!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.570
Was that here a moment ago?

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:56.730
I don't remember.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:59.190
The chair's the real murder weapon?

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.400
So now we just need the murderer's name.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.730
I have an idea about that, too.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.070
The killer...

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.650
...is you!

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.980
That's a frog.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:18.320
I believe the frog transformed into
a human and beat Chuya to death.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.860
And to, like, hide his crime or something,
he splashed around some red paint...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.900
What is "something"?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.980
And then he, like, shot his
pistol or something!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.230
Perfect.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.400
Nope.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.480
Brilliant work, peach flower boy.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.110
The corpse moved.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:39.440
That deduction was like a
mackerel floating in the sky!

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.110
Chuya!

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.070
Dazai! Dazai, wake up!

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.650
No! He's dead!

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:51.570
Yeah, looks like I'm dead.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.610
You're a corpse! Don't talk!

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.400
This is a crime.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.940
Yup. A murder.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:00.440
Who would do this to Dazai?

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.900
I know, right?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.440
Any idea who could've done it?

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.320
Do you have any enemies?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.230
Anybody who you've angered?

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:12.440
People who Dazai's angered?

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.230
Oh no! There are too many!

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.570
I couldn't possibly narrow it down.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.320
What does that mean?

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.980
Who even knows if it's murder?

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:21.400
Could be suicide, right?

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.820
Yes. Dazai attempted no less
than three lover's suicides.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.110
Two of which failed.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.480
That's not important now, is it?

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.070
Suicide?

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.650
I hadn't thought of that one.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.730
Et tu, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.900
You blew out your own
stomach with a pistol, huh?

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.610
That takes guts, especially for
a peach flower boy like you.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:46.110
The pistol may not, in fact,
be the murder weapon.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.190
Perhaps someone hit him with the chair.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.030
That's not suicide.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.280
I told you that!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.610
I was murdered!

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.730
Which means someone murdered you.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:04.030
Who could he have pissed off?

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.440
It's impossible to say.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.110
There's no end of candidates.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.940
How about Haruo Sato- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.780
If he was going to kill him,
he'd have done it years ago.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.190
Before that four-meter long letter came.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.980
True.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.530
Yasunari Kawabata- <i>sensei</i> , then?

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.730
Impossible.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:31.980
Sure, Dazai wrote no end of whiny letters
about losing the Akutagawa Prize to him.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:34.570
But he wrote plenty back.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.320
It's hard to see him as angry enough to kill.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.030
Masuji Ibuse- <i>sensei</i> , perhaps?

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:43.980
It could be Kazuo Dan, too.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:43.980
You made a lot of people mad, huh?

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.150
Well, not that many...

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.980
So I've been wondering...

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.780
What's that clam?

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.570
It's a clam.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.480
A rotten clam.

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.110
It moved.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.440
So you saw through my disguise!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.530
It talked!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:10.480
Yes, I am the clam... that killed Osamu Dazai!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.400
What?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.150
You got killed by a clam?

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.190
It stinks now that it got bigger.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:20.690
Should I turn you into rotten clams, too?

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.440
Huh?

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.980
Ango! Ango!

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:27.070
How? How could this happen?

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:29.030
Who could've done such a thing?

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.440
Right?

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:33.940
They sent me to hell,
which means they've got good taste.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:35.900
He's happy, huh?

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.860
Ango's like that.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.110
Do you remember who got you?

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:43.650
He probably got stabbed in a fight.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:46.480
I would never lose a fight.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.400
I'm not like you, Chuya!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.280
What did you say? You want to fight?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.820
Don't even try.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.900
You talk tough, but you're useless in a fight.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.070
You're a corpse and you wanna
pick a fight with me, huh?

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.400
A chair?

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.320
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.440
What?

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.030
That was a close one.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:15.650
This world is under the Taint's control.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:20.780
Was it your personal taste,
deceiving us with these ridiculous stories?

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.610
Saku- <i>kun</i> ?

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.530
"Sakutaro Hagiwara"

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.030
" <i>Howl at the Moon</i> "

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.530
The tainting continues.

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:30.230
Is everyone okay?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.820
I couldn't say.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.650
Should we go as well?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.480
No.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:42.070
If we all go and get wiped out,
there'll be no one left to do anything.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.110
Don't even say that.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:47.900
Aren't you curious, though?

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:53.360
Why can anyone delve into
this book, without restrictions?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.110
That's very unusual, right?

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.860
Yes.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.190
Do you know why, Shimazaki?

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.230
I have a theory.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.230
Will you hear it?

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:09.780
What a book seeks is a connection to an author.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.150
If it allows anyone to enter,

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:17.900
that means that the person it most
wants to connect with isn't there.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.230
If they're aren't the one you want most,
what they are makes no difference.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:29.900
I think it's similar to how a child
feels about his favorite toy.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:36.400
So the author that Sakutaro Hagiwara
wants most is someone else?

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.530
Yes.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:43.780
And that person probably holds
the key to saving this book.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:47.730
Wait, the only welcoming
committee I get is a cat?

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.780
So you came,

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:52.980
"Saisei Muro"

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:52.980
Saisei Muro?

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.230
Some of the soldiers were
of a disagreeable sort,

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.940
and likely missed the target intentionally.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.690
Who are these guys?

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:17.070
How the hell should I know?

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:22.070
When the man who'd died from the
gunshots awoke in his dreams,

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.280
sad tears fell in the sky.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:28.400
That's the kind of tobacco this is.

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.690
Wait, they're zombies?

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:35.730
On the pale white stomach of the
drunk lying face-up, dead,

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:40.650
I saw clear pale drops of blood,
and a twisted polygonal heart.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.480
The ground around him gleamed,

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:49.070
covered with severed hands
withered by rheumatism,

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:51.480
and squished guts.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:58.440
The grass was sharp.
Everything shown like radium.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:58.440
Sakutaro, I've had enough of this crap!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.150
Damn it!

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:16.320
Bamboo grew from the gleaming grass,

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:17.820
green bamboo grew,

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.070
and beneath the ground grew its roots.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:24.400
The roots thinned and came to an end,
and from the end came tiny hairs,

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.820
tiny hairs growing,

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.730
shivering slightly...

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:33.820
They just keep coming.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.230
Bamboo grew on the hard ground.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:39.230
Bamboo grew sharp upon the surface.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.530
Bamboo grew straight.

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:44.030
Chilled and frozen at its joints,

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:46.530
the bamboo grew beneath the blue sky.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:48.860
Bamboo. Bamboo. Bamboo grew.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.150
Stop it!

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:58.940
The Taint is controlling you!

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:02.570
The Taint? Controlling me?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.030
I'm not being controlled.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:18.730
I'm working with the Taint
of my own free will.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:20.650
What do you mean?

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:23.070
Your book's going to disappear!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.030
Do you understand that?

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.150
Behold, all sins are recorded.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:37.150
But not all are mine.

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:42.400
What truly appears before me is
a phantom of a shadowless flame.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.860
A sorrowful ghost,
disappearing above the snow.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.190
What use are my fervent confessions
on such a day as this?

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.820
All is but a phantom of a pale flame.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.150
Now what?

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:03.030
Sorry, but I don't think I can hold back!

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:12.820
A thieving dog howls at the
moon on a rotting pier.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.900
When the soul turns its ears to listen,

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:15.690
its miserable voice--

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.940
That's enough.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.530
I'm not interested.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.690
Death isn't to your liking?

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:23.360
You are an author, after all.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.940
And after all, you stand taller
than the other authors.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.030
Countless authors were influenced by you.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.150
Is it Saisei?

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:36.940
Saisei Muro was the finest of poets.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:41.360
The loneliness he described in <i>Poems of Love</i> ,
meant so much to me.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.230
I was in awe of the way

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:47.610
he described the mornings and
evenings that everyone experiences.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:52.400
In <i>Poems of Forgotten Spring</i> ,
he made even sighs and socks sound sad.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:55.400
I was in awe of his linguistic powers.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.530
Sai... Sai was a true master.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:15:59.650
But...

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:12.320
He abandoned poetry and
went to the world of novels.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.570
I see.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.610
And you think it's my fault?

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:19.400
No, I don't.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:23.690
It's my fault that Sai ceased to write poetry.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.570
You're amazing, Saku.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.480
What's this about?

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:33.070
Your poetry always amazes me.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.650
Your unique choice of words.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:39.400
The rhythm of your beautiful text,
like a song...

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:43.070
That's what they call god-given talent.

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:47.230
I'm sure your poems will
be read for many years,

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.690
and move many people.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.400
I can tell.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.980
Your poems are amazing too!

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:59.150
Let's keep writing wonderful
poems together, forever!

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:02.110
Sai!

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:03.980
Do your best, Saku!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.730
Novels?

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:08.230
Yup.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:10.440
I like your poetry.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.730
So why...?

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.820
Don't leave me.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.030
I'm sorry.

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:23.780
You're amazing, Saku.

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:28.440
If it weren't for me,
Saku would've kept writing.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.980
It's my fault for existing,

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.360
for writing my poems!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.860
Then what about you?

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.610
What is your goal?

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.440
I want my books to disappear.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.480
For Sai!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:02.150
The Taint's wish aligns with my own.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:05.070
You outsiders have no chance.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:06.820
I see.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:09.650
By bringing the author himself to their side,

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:14.280
the Taint gained enough
power to alter the world?

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.570
But I don't understand...

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.780
Even if your books were to disappear now,

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.400
Saisei's past wouldn't change.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.320
So why?

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:24.530
It will change.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.690
Why?

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:29.820
If my books disappear,
Sai will continue to write,

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.320
and his poems will be famous
long into the future.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:36.230
The fate of a book changes both
past and future!

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:39.900
Are you the one who told
Saku- <i>kun</i> these lies?

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:41.980
They're not lies.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:44.530
You know that.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:49.230
If there's any chance,
I want to take the risk.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.980
And if you're going to interfere,
I won't hold back!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.280
Interfere?

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:58.320
I'll leave that role to him.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.400
Sai?

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.480
Why?

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.820
Hey.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.860
It's good to see you again, Saku.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.400
So you're the Taint?

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:12.690
Stop it, Sai!

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:13.860
You don't have to do this!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.440
Of course I do.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:17.400
I'm going to protect your books.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:18.940
No, Sai.

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:20.320
I...

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:22.280
This is my wish!

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:24.400
My books should disappear!

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.110
So...

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.190
Then why did you call me?

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:32.900
That weird cat told me that
this book was calling me...

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.110
That its will was strong...

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.690
And that's why he was
able to reincarnate me.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.820
Is that true?

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.150
You wanted me to stop you, right?

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.480
No, I really...

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.780
My books really shouldn't exist!

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:50.150
Because of them, you...

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.440
Do it.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.440
Pull the trigger. Now.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.730
And remove this book from the world.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.690
Do it! Do it!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:23.030
The books you wrote contain
your feelings. Your soul.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.400
I couldn't stand them disappearing.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.070
I won't let you erase them.

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:31.780
Anyone who tries, even you...
I'll stop them!

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:34.780
But because of me, you...

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.900
That's just arrogance.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.280
It's not because of you.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.820
I was just more cut out
for writing books, that's all.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:47.230
I'm sorry, Sai. I just selfishly assumed...

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:51.030
You really are selfish.

00:20:51.030 --> 00:20:53.110
That's just like you, though.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:06.900
" <i>Howl at the Moon</i> "

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.730
Looks like you had a rough time.

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:06.900
A little.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:14.190
But we succeeded in saving the book,
and a new author, too.

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:16.110
I think it went well.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.780
It went well, huh?

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:22.110
But you've forgotten your
original goal, haven't you?

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:25.110
My memories.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:26.940
Indeed.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:32.320
Yes, I want my memories as
Ryunosuke Akutagawa, the author, back.

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:33.780
But...

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.400
If I save the books,

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:40.150
someday I'll save the people
who the books will save.

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:47.190
"Setting Sun"

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.530
I think that's very valuable on its own.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:52.980
And that's enough for now.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.960
" <i>Howl at the Moon</i> "

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:33.110
<i>Literary Gourmet</i> !

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:35.230
<i>Dreamy Cute Omelet Chapter</i> .

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:38.030
Saku, you liked this, right?

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:36.570
"Woosh"

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:40.280
I worked hard on it!

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:42.940
"Omelet Made with plenty of fresh eggs!
Change the shape, add different fillings,
the possibilities are limitless!"

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:41.280
It looks good!

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:42.940
But you need more, right?

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:45.610
Sai, your face is kind of...

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.360
I'll cast a spell on it!

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.780
Increase!

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:51.530
The omelets multiplied!

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:53.940
Eat lots, okay?

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:56.280
No! Save me!

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:00.860
"An Elegant Appetite
by Hagiwara"

00:23:58.230 --> 00:24:00.860
A dream, huh?
